{%- comment -%}
  fye-popups — every popup on the site, as blocks. Lives in footer-group.json,
  so one copy is available on every page.

  REPLACES `fye-guide-popups-group.json`, which was TWELVE sections, each
  wrapping a Klaviyo embed on Forms defaults (#202020 text, #1878B9 links).
  Build-state job 7.

  KLAVIYO IS GONE (Ed, 01/09/2026). The form here is Shopify's own
  `{% form 'contact' %}`, so a submission arrives as a normal store enquiry
  and no app is involved. Consequences worth knowing:

  1. NOTHING EMAILS THE GUIDE ANY MORE. Klaviyo used to. So the popup hands
     the file over itself, on the success panel, from `file_url`. A guide with
     no `file_url` says we will email it instead — true, because the
     submission reaches hello@ either way, but it is a manual send.
  2. Marketing consent is recorded IN THE MESSAGE, not as a list
     subscription — there is no list to subscribe to now.

  EVERYTHING IDENTIFYING GOES IN `contact[body]`. READ THIS BEFORE CHANGING
  ANY FIELD NAME.
  Custom `contact[Some name]` fields did NOT show usefully in the notification
  email — tested by Ed on 01/09/2026, who could not tell which of seven
  popups a submission had come from. The message BODY is always shown, so the
  body is where the answer belongs:

    - Liquid writes a fallback body naming the popup, so an enquiry is
      identifiable even with JavaScript off.
    - On submit, fye-ui.js REWRITES that body to fold in the popup name, the
      typed message, the journey answer and the consent answer as plain lines.

  The individual named fields are still submitted as well. That is belt and
  braces, not the mechanism — do not delete the body composition and rely on
  them again.

  HOW A POPUP IS OPENED
  Any element with `data-fye-popup="<key>"` opens the block whose `key`
  matches. `guide-download-block` and `fye-two-ways` already emit that
  attribute, so no template needed editing.

  The keys are the OLD KLAVIYO FORM IDS (V9eDYg, XMzNMS, …) because that is
  what those triggers still emit — `guide-download-block`'s setting is still
  called `klaviyo_form_id`. Renaming a setting ID is not safe, so the ID stays
  and its LABEL now says "Popup key". Change a key here and you must change it
  on the trigger in the same pass, or the button silently opens nothing.

  WHY <dialog> AND NOT THE THEME'S DRAWER PATTERN
  The one deliberate exception to §6's `data-fye-drawer` convention. A modal
  over a form needs a focus trap, a background made inert, and Escape — all
  three are free and correct with <dialog> + showModal(), and about forty
  lines of hand-rolled JS without it. Drawers stay as they are.

  Layout is the Klaviyo popup Ed signed off: photograph left at a third, form
  right, stacking to photo-on-top under 749px. Its champagne button is NOT
  carried over — buttons in this system are teal filled, sage on hover.

  THE CONTACT US POPUP (key `contact`): 25/09/2026, W275 / W417
  Ed replaced every "Book consultation" button on the site with "Contact us",
  which opens this. A popup with `show_contact` on gets a reach panel above
  the form: tap-to-call, WhatsApp, a text message, email, and the Book
  consultation button to the Google diary. Someone who would happily just ring
  is no longer made to fill in a form first.
    - The header's Book appointment buttons deliberately still go straight to
      the diary (Ed, same day): a visitor reaching for the header is ready to
      book. The contact page keeps its own row too; it already is this popup.
    - Numbers are typed as people read them ("0208 178 6687"); the tel:, sms:
      and wa.me forms are derived below, so there is one value to change.
    - Under 749px the photograph is dropped for this popup so the tap-to-act
      tiles come first, and the dialog scrolls as a whole.
  URL settings cannot carry a data attribute, so most of the rewired buttons
  open this through the `#popup-<key>` link hook in fye-ui.js: their link is
  `/pages/contact-us#popup-contact`, which is also where they land without JS.

  TWO COLUMNS (25/09/2026, the Contact us popup brief)
  A popup with `show_contact` on is now a two-column dialog above 900px:
  every way to reach us on a teal panel on the left, the form on white on the
  right. Nobody is made to fill in a form to reach a human, and someone who
  wants to ring sees the number first.
    - The photograph is not rendered for this popup at any width; the teal
      panel does the job it did. The `image` setting is left alone (dropping
      a stored value is harmless, renaming is not) and still serves every
      other popup.
    - The reach panel sits OUTSIDE the form, so it stays beside the thank-you
      panel after sending. Only the form column changes.
    - `reach_divider` is now the form column's heading ("Send us a message").
      Setting ID kept; label changed.
    - Geometry, chosen not measured: 960px max width, 400px left column (the
      email address stays on one line), 52px channel rows (56px under 560),
      36px icon tiles. Everything else is a token.
    - On teal the focus ring is ivory, not sage deep: sage deep on teal is
      about 2.7:1, under the 3:1 a focus indicator needs. Ivory is 10.1:1.
    - Under 900px it stacks, reach panel first, and the whole dialog scrolls
      as one; the close button pins on its own teal tile. Under 560px it is a
      full-screen sheet: at 390 x 844 Call and WhatsApp are on the first
      screen.
    - A failed send now reopens the popup on its error (fye-ui.js); before,
      the page reloaded with the message inside a closed dialog.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- for block in section.blocks -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign b = block.settings
    assign key = b.key | default: block.id
    assign heading = b.heading | default: 'Get in touch'
    assign btn_label = b.button_label | default: 'Send'
    assign uid = key | handleize

    comment
      The line that identifies this popup in the enquiry email. A setting, so
      the email can read differently from the on-screen heading — "Guide
      request: The Eternity Ring Guide" rather than just the title.
    endcomment
    assign email_line = b.email_subject | default: heading

    comment
      THERE IS DELIBERATELY NO return_to. 01/09/2026: setting one made Shopify
      redirect to our own URL, which does not carry Shopify's contact_posted
      marker — and form.posted_successfully? is driven by that marker, so the
      success panel never rendered and the popup reopened on a blank form. It
      also dropped preview_theme_id, landing preview tests on the live theme.

      Shopify's default returns to this exact URL, marker intact, query string
      preserved. Which popup was submitted is remembered by fye-ui.js in
      sessionStorage, because the redirect carries no popup key.
    endcomment
    assign journey_list = b.journey_options | split: ','

    comment
      Reach panel (Contact us popup). UK numbers are entered as read; a
      leading 0 becomes +44 for tel: and sms:, and 44 for wa.me.
    endcomment
    assign has_reach = false
    if b.show_contact
      assign has_reach = true
    endif
    assign tel = b.phone | remove: ' '
    assign tel_first = tel | slice: 0
    if tel_first == '0'
      assign tel = tel | remove_first: '0' | prepend: '+44'
    endif
    assign mob = b.mobile | remove: ' '
    assign mob_first = mob | slice: 0
    if mob_first == '0'
      assign mob = mob | remove_first: '0' | prepend: '+44'
    endif
    assign wa = mob | remove: '+'

    comment
      The Contact us popup has no photograph at any width: the teal reach
      panel replaces it.
    endcomment
    assign show_media = false
    if b.image != blank and has_reach == false
      assign show_media = true
    endif
  -%}

  <dialog class="pop{% if has_reach %} pop--reach{% endif %}" id="fye-popup-{{ uid }}"
          data-fye-popup-panel="{{ key }}"
          data-fye-popup-label="{{ email_line | escape }}"
          aria-label="{{ heading | escape }}" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>

    {%- if has_reach -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Outside .pop__in so it can pin (sticky) while the stacked dialog
        scrolls on tablet and phone. Zero height, so it takes no layout.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="pop__bar">
        <button class="pop__close" type="button" data-fye-popup-close aria-label="Close">
          {%- render 'icon', name: 'close', size: 18 -%}
        </button>
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    <div class="pop__in{% if show_media == false and has_reach == false %} pop__in--noimage{% endif %}{% if has_reach %} pop__in--reach{% endif %}">

      {%- if show_media -%}
        <div class="pop__media">
          {{ b.image | image_url: width: 900 | image_tag:
             loading: 'lazy',
             widths: '380, 560, 760, 900',
             sizes: '(max-width: 749px) 100vw, 260px',
             alt: b.image_alt }}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if has_reach -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Tile labels are structural names for the channel, like "Home" in a
          breadcrumb; the values are settings.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="pop__reach">
          {%- if b.eyebrow != blank -%}
            <p class="eyebrow">{{ b.eyebrow }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}
          <p class="pop__title" role="heading" aria-level="2">{{ heading }}</p>
          {%- if b.intro != blank -%}
            <div class="pop__intro">{{ b.intro }}</div>
          {%- endif -%}

          <ul class="pop__ways">
            {%- if b.phone != blank -%}
              <li><a class="pop__way" href="tel:{{ tel }}">
                <span class="pop__way-icon">{%- render 'icon', name: 'phone', size: 18 -%}</span>
                <span class="pop__way-text"><span class="pop__way-label">Call</span>{{ b.phone }}</span>
                <span class="pop__way-go">{%- render 'icon', name: 'arrow-right', size: 16 -%}</span>
              </a></li>
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- if b.mobile != blank -%}
              <li><a class="pop__way" href="https://wa.me/{{ wa }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                <span class="pop__way-icon">{%- render 'icon', name: 'message', size: 18 -%}</span>
                <span class="pop__way-text"><span class="pop__way-label">WhatsApp</span>{{ b.mobile }}</span>
                <span class="pop__way-go">{%- render 'icon', name: 'arrow-right', size: 16 -%}</span>
                <span class="visually-hidden">(opens in a new tab)</span>
              </a></li>
              <li><a class="pop__way" href="sms:{{ mob }}">
                <span class="pop__way-icon">{%- render 'icon', name: 'sms', size: 18 -%}</span>
                <span class="pop__way-text"><span class="pop__way-label">Text us</span>{{ b.mobile }}</span>
                <span class="pop__way-go">{%- render 'icon', name: 'arrow-right', size: 16 -%}</span>
              </a></li>
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- if b.email != blank -%}
              <li><a class="pop__way" href="mailto:{{ b.email }}">
                <span class="pop__way-icon">{%- render 'icon', name: 'mail', size: 18 -%}</span>
                <span class="pop__way-text"><span class="pop__way-label">Email</span>{{ b.email }}</span>
                <span class="pop__way-go">{%- render 'icon', name: 'arrow-right', size: 16 -%}</span>
              </a></li>
            {%- endif -%}
          </ul>

          {%- if b.hours != blank -%}
            <p class="pop__hours">{{ b.hours }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- if b.book_url != blank -%}
            <div class="pop__book">
              <a class="btn btn--block" href="{{ b.book_url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                {%- render 'icon', name: 'calendar', size: 18 -%}
                {{ b.book_label | default: 'Book consultation' }}
                <span class="visually-hidden">(opens in a new tab)</span>
              </a>
              {%- if b.book_note != blank -%}
                <p class="pop__book-note">{{ b.book_note }}</p>
              {%- endif -%}
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

      <div class="pop__body">
        {%- unless has_reach -%}
          <button class="pop__close" type="button" data-fye-popup-close aria-label="Close">
            {%- render 'icon', name: 'close', size: 18 -%}
          </button>
        {%- endunless -%}

        {%- assign form_id = 'pop-form-' | append: key | handleize -%}
      {%- form 'contact', id: form_id, class: 'pop__form' -%}

          {%- if form.posted_successfully? -%}

            {%- comment -%}
              Rendered on every popup after any successful contact submission —
              the flash is not per-form. Harmless: only the popup named in the
              query string is opened, and the others stay closed.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <div class="pop__done" data-fye-popup-done tabindex="-1">
              {%- if has_reach -%}
                <span class="pop__done-mark">{%- render 'icon', name: 'check', size: 22 -%}</span>
              {%- else -%}
                <p class="eyebrow">{{ b.eyebrow | default: 'For Your Eternity' }}</p>
              {%- endif -%}
              <p class="pop__title" role="heading" aria-level="2">{{ b.success_heading | default: 'Thank you' }}</p>
              <div class="pop__intro">{{ b.success_body | default: '<p>We have your details.</p>' }}</div>

              {%- if b.file_url != blank -%}
                <a class="btn btn--block" href="{{ b.file_url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                  {%- render 'icon', name: 'download', size: 18 -%}
                  {{ b.download_label | default: 'Download the guide' }}
                </a>
              {%- elsif b.no_file_note != blank -%}
                <p class="pop__note">{{ b.no_file_note }}</p>
              {%- endif -%}

              {%- if has_reach -%}
                <button class="btn btn--outline" type="button" data-fye-popup-close>Close</button>
              {%- endif -%}
            </div>

          {%- else -%}

            {%- if has_reach -%}
              {%- if b.reach_divider != blank -%}
                <p class="pop__formtitle" role="heading" aria-level="3">{{ b.reach_divider }}</p>
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- else -%}
              {%- if b.eyebrow != blank -%}
                <p class="eyebrow">{{ b.eyebrow }}</p>
              {%- endif -%}
              <p class="pop__title" role="heading" aria-level="2">{{ heading }}</p>
              {%- if b.intro != blank -%}
                <div class="pop__intro">{{ b.intro }}</div>
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endif -%}

            {%- if form.errors -%}
              {%- comment -%}
                Shopify's single message, above the fields. data-fye-popup-error
                is what makes fye-ui.js reopen the popup and focus this.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              <div class="pop__errors" id="pop-err-{{ uid }}" role="alert" tabindex="-1" data-fye-popup-error>
                <p>{{ form.errors | default_errors }}</p>
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}

            <div class="pop__pair">
              <div class="pop__field">
                <label for="pop-first-{{ uid }}">First name</label>
                <input id="pop-first-{{ uid }}" type="text" name="contact[First name]" autocomplete="given-name" placeholder="First name">
              </div>
              <div class="pop__field">
                <label for="pop-last-{{ uid }}">Last name</label>
                <input id="pop-last-{{ uid }}" type="text" name="contact[Last name]" autocomplete="family-name" placeholder="Last name">
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="pop__pair">
              <div class="pop__field">
                <label for="pop-email-{{ uid }}">Email address</label>
                <input id="pop-email-{{ uid }}" type="email" name="contact[email]" autocomplete="email" placeholder="you@email.com" required
                       {%- if form.errors contains 'email' %} aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="pop-err-{{ uid }}"{% endif %}>
              </div>
              <div class="pop__field">
                <label for="pop-phone-{{ uid }}">Telephone <span class="pop__opt">(optional)</span></label>
                <input id="pop-phone-{{ uid }}" type="tel" name="contact[Telephone]" autocomplete="tel" placeholder="For a personal follow-up">
              </div>
            </div>

            {%- if b.show_journey and journey_list.size > 0 -%}
              <div class="pop__field">
                <label for="pop-journey-{{ uid }}">{{ b.journey_label | default: 'Where you are in your journey' }}</label>
                <select id="pop-journey-{{ uid }}" name="contact[Journey]" data-fye-popup-journey>
                  <option value="">Please choose…</option>
                  {%- for opt in journey_list -%}
                    {%- assign opt_clean = opt | strip -%}
                    <option value="{{ opt_clean | escape }}">{{ opt_clean }}</option>
                  {%- endfor -%}
                </select>
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}

            {%- comment -%}
              The message box. On an enquiry it is the whole point; on a guide
              request it is noise, so it is a per-popup switch.

              It is NOT named contact[body] — the body is composed on submit
              and would overwrite whatever was typed here. fye-ui.js folds this
              value into the body instead.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- if b.show_message -%}
              <div class="pop__field">
                <label for="pop-message-{{ uid }}">{{ b.message_label | default: 'What can we help with?' }}</label>
                <textarea id="pop-message-{{ uid }}" name="contact[Message]" rows="{% if has_reach %}3{% else %}4{% endif %}" data-fye-popup-message
                          placeholder="{{ b.message_placeholder | default: 'A piece you have seen, a budget, a date to work to…' | escape }}"></textarea>
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}

            {%- if b.show_consent -%}
              <label class="pop__consent" for="pop-consent-{{ uid }}">
                <input id="pop-consent-{{ uid }}" type="checkbox" name="contact[Happy to be emailed]" value="Yes" data-fye-popup-consent>
                <span>{{ b.consent_text | default: "Yes, I'm happy for For Your Eternity to email me occasional news. I can unsubscribe anytime." }}</span>
              </label>
            {%- endif -%}

            {%- comment -%}
              THE field that makes an enquiry identifiable. Liquid writes a
              usable fallback; fye-ui.js rewrites it on submit with the typed
              message and the answers folded in. Never remove the value here —
              it is what a visitor with JavaScript off sends.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <input type="hidden" name="contact[body]" value="{{ email_line | escape }} (sent from {{ request.path }})" data-fye-popup-body>

            <div class="pop__send">
              <button class="btn btn--block pop__submit" type="submit">{{ btn_label }}</button>
              {%- if b.reassurance != blank -%}
                <p class="pop__note">{{ b.reassurance }}</p>
              {%- endif -%}
            </div>

          {%- endif -%}

        {%- endform -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  </dialog>
{%- endfor -%}

{% stylesheet %}
/* ---- the dialog itself -------------------------------------------------- */
.fye .pop {
  width: min(760px, calc(100vw - (2 * var(--pad-x))));
  max-width: none;
  max-height: calc(100vh - (2 * var(--s8)));
  padding: 0;
  border: 0;
  border-radius: var(--radius);
  background: var(--white);
  color: var(--ink);
  overflow: hidden;
}
/* ::backdrop does not reliably inherit custom properties across engines, so
   the token's value is repeated as a fallback. */
.fye .pop::backdrop { background: var(--scrim, rgba(35, 61, 71, 0.42)); }
.fye dialog.pop:not([open]) { display: none; }

/* A third to the photograph, as the signed-off design. */
.fye .pop__in { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 260px 1fr; min-height: 0; }
.fye .pop__in--noimage { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }

.fye .pop__media { position: relative; background: var(--ivory); }
.fye .pop__media :where(img) { position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; }

.fye .pop__body {
  position: relative;
  padding: var(--s7);
  overflow-y: auto;
  max-height: calc(100vh - (2 * var(--s8)));
}

.fye .pop__close {
  position: absolute;
  top: var(--s3);
  right: var(--s3);
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  width: 44px;
  height: 44px;
  padding: 0;
  border: 0;
  background: none;
  color: var(--ink);
  transition: color var(--dur) var(--ease);
}
.fye .pop__close:hover { color: var(--sage); }

/* ---- words -------------------------------------------------------------- */
/* A <p role="heading">, not an <h2> (audit 02/09/2026, S3/P2): every popup
   is in the HTML of every page, so nine dialogs put eighteen h2s into every
   page's outline and into fye-ui.js's contents lists, which are built from
   the page's h2s. The role keeps it a heading for screen readers inside the
   dialog. The declarations below restate fye-core's :where(h2) base so it
   renders exactly as the h2 did. */
.fye .pop__title {
  margin: var(--s2) 0 var(--s3);
  font-family: var(--font-display);
  font-size: var(--fs-h3);
  font-weight: var(--fw-regular);
  letter-spacing: var(--tr-h2);
  line-height: var(--lh-heading);
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--ink);
  text-wrap: pretty;
}
.fye .pop__intro { margin-bottom: var(--s5); font-size: var(--fs-small); line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink-soft); }
.fye .pop__intro :where(p:last-child) { margin-bottom: 0; }

/* ---- fields ------------------------------------------------------------- */
/* Inputs, selects, textareas and the 48px minimum come from fye-core's form
   rules; only the stacking and the pair are this section's business. */
.fye .pop__form { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--s4); }
.fye .pop__field { display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
.fye .pop__pair { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: var(--s4); }
.fye .pop__opt { font-weight: var(--fw-light); letter-spacing: 0; text-transform: none; }
/* Shorter than the site default: a popup has to stay on screen. */
.fye .pop__field :where(textarea) { min-height: 96px; }

/* The consent line is sentence case and small — the only label in the theme
   that is not an uppercase field label, because it is a sentence the visitor
   reads, not a name for a box. */
.fye .pop__consent {
  display: flex;
  align-items: flex-start;
  gap: var(--s3);
  margin: 0;
  font-size: var(--fs-fine);
  font-weight: var(--fw-light);
  letter-spacing: 0;
  line-height: 1.5;
  text-transform: none;
  color: var(--ink-soft);
}
.fye .pop__consent input {
  flex: 0 0 18px;
  width: 18px;
  height: 18px;
  min-height: 0;
  margin-top: 2px;
  accent-color: var(--teal);
}

.fye .pop__submit { margin-top: var(--s2); }
.fye .pop__note { margin: 0; font-size: var(--fs-fine); line-height: 1.5; color: var(--ink-soft); text-align: center; }

.fye .pop__errors {
  padding: var(--s3) var(--s4);
  background: var(--mist);
  font-size: var(--fs-small);
}
.fye .pop__errors :where(p) { margin: 0; }

/* ---- success ------------------------------------------------------------ */
.fye .pop__done { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--s3); }
.fye .pop__done .btn { margin-top: var(--s3); }

/* ---- send row: button, then the reassurance line ------------------------ */
.fye .pop__send { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--s4); margin-top: var(--s2); }
.fye .pop__send .pop__submit { margin-top: 0; }

.fye .pop__errors:focus { outline: var(--focus-ring); outline-offset: 2px; }

/* ---- reflow: 749, the theme's own middle breakpoint --------------------- */
@media (max-width: 749px) {
  .fye .pop__in { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  .fye .pop__media { height: 180px; }
  .fye .pop__media :where(img) { position: static; height: 180px; }
  .fye .pop__body { padding: var(--s5); }
}
@media (max-width: 560px) {
  .fye .pop__pair { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
}

/* ============================================================================
   CONTACT US: TWO COLUMNS (25/09/2026). Reach panel left on teal, form right
   on white. Everything below is scoped to .pop--reach / .pop__reach, so the
   guide and bespoke popups are untouched. Geometry literals are chosen, not
   measured; see the file comment.
   ========================================================================== */
.fye .pop--reach { width: min(960px, calc(100vw - (2 * var(--pad-x)))); }
.fye .pop__in--reach { grid-template-columns: 400px minmax(0, 1fr); }

.fye .pop__bar {
  position: absolute;
  top: var(--s2);
  right: var(--s2);
  z-index: 2;
  display: flex;
  justify-content: flex-end;
  height: 0;
}
.fye .pop__bar .pop__close { position: static; }
.fye .pop__close:active { color: var(--sage-deep); }

/* ---- left: every way to reach us ---------------------------------------- */
.fye .pop__reach {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  padding: var(--s7);
  background: var(--teal);
  color: var(--on-dark);
  overflow: hidden;              /* the fast path never scrolls on desktop */
}
.fye .pop__reach .eyebrow { margin-bottom: var(--s2); color: var(--on-dark-soft); }
.fye .pop__reach .pop__title { margin: 0 0 var(--s3); color: var(--on-dark); }
.fye .pop__reach .pop__intro { margin-bottom: var(--s5); color: var(--on-dark); font-weight: var(--fw-light); line-height: 1.5; }
.fye .pop__reach :focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--ivory); outline-offset: 2px; }

.fye .pop__ways {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
  list-style: none;
  border-top: 1px solid var(--line-on-dark);
}
.fye .pop__ways > li { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-on-dark); }
.fye .pop__way {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: var(--s3);
  min-height: 52px;
  padding: var(--s1) 0;
  color: var(--on-dark);
  font-size: var(--fs-small);
  line-height: 1.35;
  text-decoration: none;
}
.fye .pop__way-icon {
  display: flex;
  flex: 0 0 36px;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  height: 36px;
  border: 1px solid var(--line-on-dark);
  transition: background var(--dur) var(--ease), border-color var(--dur) var(--ease), color var(--dur) var(--ease);
}
.fye .pop__way-text { display: flex; flex: 1; flex-direction: column; gap: 2px; min-width: 0; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
.fye .pop__way-label {
  font-size: var(--fs-eyebrow);
  font-weight: var(--fw-medium);
  letter-spacing: var(--tr-eyebrow);
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--on-dark-soft);
}
.fye .pop__way-go { display: flex; opacity: 0; transition: opacity var(--dur) var(--ease); }
.fye .pop__way:hover .pop__way-icon { background: var(--sage); border-color: var(--sage); color: var(--teal); }
.fye .pop__way:active .pop__way-icon { background: var(--sage-deep); border-color: var(--sage-deep); color: var(--on-dark); }
.fye .pop__way:hover .pop__way-go,
.fye .pop__way:focus-visible .pop__way-go { opacity: 1; }

.fye .pop__hours { margin: var(--s3) 0 0; font-size: var(--fs-fine); line-height: 1.4; color: var(--on-dark-soft); }

/* Filled on teal is ivory, as on .band--teal. The panel is not a band, so the
   band rule does not reach it and is restated here. */
.fye .pop__book { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--s2); margin-top: auto; padding-top: var(--s5); }
.fye .pop__book .btn { background: var(--ivory); border-color: var(--ivory); color: var(--teal); }
.fye .pop__book .btn:hover { background: var(--sage); border-color: var(--sage); color: var(--teal); }
.fye .pop__book .btn:active { background: var(--sage-deep); border-color: var(--sage-deep); color: var(--ivory); }
.fye .pop__book-note { margin: 0; font-size: var(--fs-fine); line-height: 1.4; color: var(--on-dark-soft); }

/* ---- right: the form ---------------------------------------------------- */
.fye .pop--reach .pop__body { padding: var(--s7) var(--s9) var(--s7) var(--s7); overscroll-behavior: contain; }
.fye .pop__formtitle {
  margin: 0 0 var(--s1);
  font-family: var(--font-display);
  font-size: var(--fs-h4);
  font-weight: var(--fw-regular);
  letter-spacing: var(--tr-h2);
  line-height: var(--lh-heading);
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--ink);
}
.fye .pop--reach .pop__form { gap: var(--s3); }
/* Core's field focus is a sage border only, under 3:1 on white. This popup
   is the main conversion point, so it gets the full ring. */
.fye .pop--reach :where(input, select, textarea):focus-visible { outline: var(--focus-ring); outline-offset: 2px; border-color: var(--teal); }
.fye .pop--reach :where(input[aria-invalid='true']) { border-color: var(--teal); }
.fye .pop--reach .pop__send { flex-direction: row; align-items: center; gap: var(--s5); margin-top: var(--s1); }
.fye .pop--reach .pop__send .btn { flex: none; width: auto; }
.fye .pop--reach .pop__send .pop__note { max-width: 30ch; text-align: left; }

/* ---- thank you: the form column only; the reach panel stays -------------- */
.fye .pop--reach .pop__done { align-items: flex-start; gap: var(--s4); padding-block: var(--s10); }
.fye .pop--reach .pop__done:focus { outline: none; }
.fye .pop--reach .pop__done .pop__intro { margin: 0; max-width: 34ch; font-size: var(--fs-body); font-weight: var(--fw-light); color: var(--ink); }
.fye .pop--reach .pop__done .btn { margin-top: var(--s2); }
.fye .pop__done-mark {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  width: 48px;
  height: 48px;
  border: var(--hairline);
  color: var(--teal);
}

/* ---- 900: one column, reach first, the whole dialog scrolls as one ------- */
@media (max-width: 900px) {
  .fye .pop--reach { overflow-y: auto; overscroll-behavior: contain; }
  .fye .pop__in--reach { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  .fye .pop--reach .pop__bar { position: sticky; top: 0; right: auto; padding: var(--s2) var(--s2) 0 0; }
  /* Its own teal tile, so it reads over the teal panel and the white form. */
  .fye .pop--reach .pop__close { background: var(--teal); color: var(--on-dark); transition: background var(--dur) var(--ease), color var(--dur) var(--ease); }
  .fye .pop--reach .pop__close:hover { background: var(--sage); color: var(--teal); }
  .fye .pop--reach .pop__close:active { background: var(--sage-deep); color: var(--on-dark); }
  .fye .pop--reach .pop__close:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--ivory); outline-offset: -4px; }
  .fye .pop__reach { padding: var(--s8) var(--s8) var(--s7); overflow: visible; }
  .fye .pop__reach .pop__intro { max-width: 56ch; }
  .fye .pop__ways { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); column-gap: var(--s6); }
  .fye .pop__book { flex-direction: row; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: var(--s5); margin-top: 0; }
  .fye .pop__book .btn { width: auto; }
  .fye .pop--reach .pop__body { max-height: none; overflow: visible; padding: var(--s7) var(--s8) var(--s8); }
  .fye .pop--reach .pop__done { padding-block: var(--s4); }
}

/* ---- 560: full-screen sheet; rows and pairs stack ----------------------- */
@media (max-width: 560px) {
  .fye .pop--reach { width: 100%; max-width: 100%; height: 100%; max-height: 100%; margin: 0; }
  .fye .pop__reach { padding: var(--s6); }
  .fye .pop__reach .pop__title { margin-bottom: var(--s2); padding-right: var(--s8); }
  .fye .pop__reach .pop__intro { margin-bottom: var(--s4); }
  .fye .pop__ways { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  .fye .pop__way { min-height: 56px; }
  .fye .pop__way-go { opacity: 1; }   /* no hover on touch: show the affordance */
  .fye .pop__book { flex-direction: column; align-items: stretch; gap: var(--s2); }
  .fye .pop__book .btn { width: 100%; }
  .fye .pop--reach .pop__body { padding: var(--s7) var(--s6) var(--s8); }
  .fye .pop--reach .pop__send { flex-direction: column; align-items: stretch; gap: var(--s3); }
  .fye .pop--reach .pop__send .btn { width: 100%; }
  .fye .pop--reach .pop__send .pop__note { max-width: none; }
}

/* ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   TOUCH TARGETS AND MINIMUM TYPE — 02/09/2026, from the first smoke run with
   a dialog open. Both faults were fixed on the contact page a few hours
   earlier; the two forms share markup by descent but not CSS, so neither fix
   travelled.
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------- */

/* An 18px checkbox is correct — the LABEL is the tap target, so it carries the
   44px minimum. */
.fye .pop__consent {
  min-height: 44px;
  padding-block: var(--s1);
}

/* Sentence case inside an uppercase label, so it does not get the 11px
   micro-label allowance — 12px is the floor for anything read as words. */
.fye .pop__opt {
  font-size: 12px;
}
{% endstylesheet %}

